# .dockerignore — the build-context filter for every image built from THIS
# directory. Eight compose services (`api`, `prober`, `correlation`,
# `frontend`, `nginx`, `mock-nms`, `mock-servicenow`, `secrets-seal`) declare
# `context: ../..` from deployment/docker/, which resolves here — so without
# this file the context is the whole working tree, `data/` (double-digit GB of
# live OpenSearch/ClickHouse/VictoriaMetrics state) included.
#
# Two things it buys, both of which the tracker row (#193) called out:
#   1. Cost — the daemon stops receiving gigabytes it can never use, and an
#      unrelated write under data/ stops invalidating every image's cache.
#   2. Safety — nothing under data/ or backups/ (live state, pre-cutover
#      snapshots), no `.env`, and no key material can reach an image, today or
#      the day a Dockerfile gains a broader COPY.
#
# RULE FOR EDITING THIS FILE: never exclude a path a Dockerfile COPYs.
# `tests/test_dockerignore_copy_sources.py` parses every
# deployment/docker/Dockerfile* COPY line and fails if this file would ignore
# one — run it after any change here or to a COPY line. The non-obvious ones it
# protects: `src/frontend/dist` and `docs-portal/build` are BUILD OUTPUT that
# the frontend image ships (both gitignored, neither dockerignorable), and
# `NOTICE` + two files under docs/ are the licence texts the images carry.

# ---- version control, CI metadata, agent scratch ---------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude

# ---- live runtime state and local artefacts (never an image input) ---------
data
backups
# Release bundles built by `make bundle`. This matches the TOP-LEVEL dist/ only
# (Docker patterns match the whole relative path) — src/frontend/dist, which the
# frontend image ships, is a different path and stays in the context.
dist
compliance
telemetry-catalog
tests
scripts
docs-portal/node_modules
docs-portal/.docusaurus

# ---- secrets: generated env files and key material -------------------------
# `.env` is generated at install and holds every stack credential.
deployment/docker/.env
deployment/docker/.env.*
deployment/docker/nginx/certs
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*

# ---- dependency trees, caches and compiled artefacts -----------------------
# src/backend/vendor is deliberately NOT here: the Go build is offline and needs it.
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.tox
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Stray `go build -o api` output in the source tree (gitignored, 40+ MB).
src/backend/api
src/backend/backend
src/backend/*.test
src/correlation/build

# ---- logs, temp files, editor / OS droppings -------------------------------
**/*.log
**/*.swp
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
tmp
.tmp
